      "title": "Addressing Unauthorized Access Attempts and Suspicious Login Activity in Subscription Manager",
      "content_summary": "Guidance for investigating unauthorized access attempts, account lockouts, and unexpected logout events caused by improper access reviews or operator errors.",
      "content_body": "When users report access denied errors or unexpected logouts, first verify that the incident is not due to a known product limitation regarding session timeout configurations. Check the audit logs for elevated privilege changes; if entries are missing, it often indicates an improper access review process or operator error during role assignment. To resolve persistent suspicious login activity, perform a comprehensive access review to ensure permissions align with current job roles. Apply a configuration change to adjust session retention policies if the behavior is consistent with default security settings, or update permissions directly to remove unnecessary elevated access."
